{"w":2400,"h":3106,"lines":[{"x":0.80250903528814965,"t":"Reading","h":0.020227149771784303,"y":0.044717228490980365,"c":1,"w":0.085017058054606132},{"w":0.47256169637044276,"t":"READING PASSAGE 2 FB.com\/LouisQuang Vo","x":0.06716478824023886,"y":0.082971610229991666,"h":0.0320277315374351,"c":1},{"w":0.80856730143229161,"h":0.030709747491309725,"y":0.12782958339090522,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading","x":0.067561142293431548,"c":1},{"x":0.066448551027249517,"y":0.14845128140011687,"c":1,"w":0.15623952229817706,"h":0.025701686173811744,"t":"Passage 2 below."},{"t":"SAVING THE SOIL","h":0.0264459304170922,"x":0.3378129834024679,"y":0.18960850364717385,"w":0.26995531717936194,"c":1},{"w":0.73919097900390618,"c":1,"y":0.23256959263984689,"x":0.10318381417350793,"h":0.029342140448300635,"t":"More than a third of the Earth's top layer is at risk. Is there hope for our planet's"},{"x":0.35508325499513915,"y":0.25495207340288939,"w":0.23721257527669271,"h":0.019868495766761862,"t":"most precious resource?","c":1},{"y":0.29282528789370899,"h":0.024571619568067637,"c":1,"w":0.81780075073242187,"x":0.065741986930802715,"t":"A More than a third of the world's soil is endangered, according to a recent UN report."},{"t":"If we don't slow the decline, all farmable soil could be gone in 60 years. Since soil","x":0.10505192646704377,"w":0.7654280598958334,"h":0.028740865065064347,"y":0.31002447333776073,"c":1},{"y":0.3335091913486633,"t":"grows 95% of our food, and sustains human life in other more surprising ways, that","x":0.10520934494305152,"w":0.77455108642578119,"c":1,"h":0.022848744585831859},{"t":"is a huge problem.","y":0.35387384263873356,"x":0.10311154270027131,"w":0.17717177073160809,"h":0.020693149554368628,"c":1},{"h":0.021205781738910079,"c":1,"x":0.10520624419754077,"w":0.75576792399088555,"y":0.38305440586518058,"t":"Peter Groffman, from the Cary Institute of Ecosystem Studies in New York, points"},{"x":0.10521089743628674,"c":1,"y":0.40350043524474899,"t":"out that soil scientists have been warning about the degradation of the world's soil","h":0.020138921694684897,"w":0.76326843261718746},{"t":"for decades. At the same time, our understanding of its importance to humans has","x":0.10338347450947927,"w":0.76691726684570316,"y":0.42296511610439735,"h":0.018895348808647183,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.020605280103026424,"y":0.4417256923541375,"t":"grown. A single gram of healthy soil might contain 100 million bacteria, as well as","x":0.1052631763945998,"w":0.75375935872395838},{"y":0.46361880255709287,"w":0.74812032063802092,"h":0.018995492594977348,"x":0.10714284714640314,"c":1,"t":"other microorganisms such as viruses and fungi, living amid decomposing plants"},{"y":0.48260173637120285,"t":"and various minerals.","w":0.20146170298258465,"x":0.10699369829381034,"c":1,"h":0.01748445858436487},{"y":0.51308139536052988,"w":0.72932332356770835,"c":1,"h":0.018895348808647183,"t":"That means soils do not just grow our food, but are the source of nearly all our","x":0.10714284939494897},{"x":0.10700531333546488,"t":"existing antibiotics, and could be our best hope in the fight against antibiotic-","w":0.712662607828776,"c":1,"y":0.52911840935235399,"h":0.024335852608861841},{"h":0.02089619805409082,"t":"resistant bacteria. Soil is also an ally against climate change: as microorganisms","x":0.1052082522345458,"w":0.75011739095052077,"c":1,"y":0.54930237433272011},{"y":0.56910635259387887,"h":0.022111760057791918,"t":"within soil digest dead animals and plants, they lock in their carbon content, holding","w":0.7745669555664062,"c":1,"x":0.10708187020058556},{"y":0.58810925482088172,"w":0.75395619710286466,"c":1,"t":"three times the amount of carbon as does the entire atmosphere. Soils also store","h":0.023722474834493745,"x":0.10706437854171355},{"c":1,"h":0.022161543944998141,"w":0.7727341206868491,"x":0.10706425468326065,"y":0.60742821415017612,"t":"water, preventing flood damage: in the UK, damage to buildings, roads and bridges"},{"h":0.018895348808647183,"x":0.10714285970201085,"w":0.64473683675130211,"c":1,"t":"from floods caused by soil degradation costs £233 million every year.","y":0.62936046512708665},{"h":0.020421839343756965,"t":"C If the soil loses its ability to perform these functions, the human race could be in","x":0.069548878586318974,"y":0.65697674434063813,"w":0.78007517496744794,"c":1},{"t":"big trouble. The danger is not that the soil will disappear completely, but that the","x":0.10902256738563598,"y":0.67732558140718224,"h":0.018895348808647294,"w":0.74248118082682291,"c":1},{"x":0.10896752553414492,"y":0.69470536474783606,"c":1,"h":0.022093820172743972,"t":"microorganisms that give it its special properties will be lost. And once this has","w":0.72943262736002601},{"x":0.10894649414454145,"y":0.71508654855700882,"h":0.021638504244478329,"c":1,"w":0.56780303955078126,"t":"happened, it may take the soil thousands of years to recover."},{"t":"Agriculture is by far the biggest problem. In the wild, when plants grow they remove","y":0.7440437858453165,"w":0.77255640665690106,"h":0.02060528071711154,"x":0.11090224767283795,"c":1},{"x":0.11090224444793459,"y":0.76453488387506419,"t":"nutrients from the soil, but then when the plants die and decay these nutrients are","c":1,"w":0.75751881917317709,"h":0.020397504989515869},{"t":"returned directly to the soil. Humans tend not to return unused parts of harvested","y":0.78294252256590002,"x":0.11085171254838296,"w":0.75010813395182285,"h":0.018583096309546465,"c":1},{"t":"crops directly to the soil to enrich it, meaning that the soil gradually becomes","x":0.11268507966493341,"y":0.79977166225590735,"h":0.022335881505255006,"w":0.70697245279947918,"c":1},{"h":0.018995492594977459,"y":0.81970379912378133,"w":0.73684209187825522,"t":"less fertile. In the past we developed strategies to get around the problem, such","x":0.11090226601575959,"c":1},{"y":0.83715875677526996,"t":"as regularly varying the types of crops grown, or leaving fields uncultivated for a","x":0.11269398264244596,"w":0.73520721435546865,"h":0.025839297754566504,"c":1},{"x":0.11210973294196816,"c":1,"t":"season.","y":0.85980260769825689,"w":0.076626885732014982,"h":0.01701362226674108},{"y":0.88660210280544549,"h":0.020223333846348335,"x":0.11272999177077167,"c":1,"t":"But these practices became inconvenient as populations grew and agriculture had","w":0.75760416666666663},{"y":0.90545496517186863,"x":0.11273008064755705,"w":0.76135950724283852,"h":0.019847810306782399,"c":1,"t":"to be run on more commercial lines. A solution came in the early 20th century with"},{"y":0.92433998701929132,"w":0.76691731770833338,"c":1,"t":"the Haber-Bosch process for manufacturing ammonium nitrate. Farmers have been","h":0.018995492594977459,"x":0.1146616417986281},{"t":"putting this synthetic fertiliser on their fields ever since.","y":0.94317777837055938,"w":0.50392562866210944,"h":0.020588745244917162,"c":1,"x":0.11457863681050043},{"w":0.028195489247640038,"y":0.9825581397177453,"h":0.015988371407532731,"t":"85","c":1,"x":0.85714285689873648}]}